<title>UK: BT gains as SBC Warburg repeats &quot;buy&quot;.</title>
<headline>BT gains as SBC Warburg repeats &quot;buy&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Telecommunications Plc shares rose on Tuesday as SBC Warburg repeated a &quot;buy&quot; on the stock following a U.S. briefing by MCI Communications Corp, BT's planned merger partner, dealers said.</p>
<p>The stock was up 5-1/2p at 433 by 0954 GMT in active trade of 4.5 million shares.  </p>
<p>Warburg said there were signs that MCI's lead in integrated services was improving its results in long-distance operations, while recent results at the Avantel and MCI Systemhouse units were also promising, dealers said.</p>
<p>Analysts at Warburg were not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
</text>
